{"id": "EUVD-2026-27639", "enisaUuid": "e104087b-55af-3ced-b094-709b81a6954b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsrcu: Use irq_work to start GP in tiny SRCU\n\nTiny SRCU's srcu_gp_start_if_needed() directly calls schedule_work(),\nwhich acquires the workqueue pool->lock.\n\nThis causes a lockdep splat when call_srcu() is called with a scheduler\nlock held, due to:\n\n  call_srcu() [holding pi_lock]\n    srcu_gp_start_if_needed()\n      schedule_work() -> pool->lock\n\n  workqueue_init() / create_worker() [holding pool->lock]\n    wake_up_process() -> try_to_wake_up() -> pi_lock\n\nAlso add irq_work_sync() to cleanup_srcu_struct() to prevent a\nuse-after-free if a queued irq_work fires after cleanup begins.\n\nTested with rcutorture SRCU-T and no lockdep warnings.\n\n[ Thanks to Boqun for similar fix in patch \"rcu: Use an intermediate irq_work\nto start process_srcu()\" ]", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T07:40:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20b98d9ffb09763048a7c84b47403eb0f177272c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2127e6b79d9d579ea538a350d1bbe859e39814d5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28768bc7ea0b13f558a70f63cc3cfcd32d55d488", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb37286db65368cb72ba8757ad86299c4e4a73fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6fc88b22bc8d12ad52e8412c667ec0f5bf055af"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43115", "GHSA-vj6f-v49f-r83x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08750772-a0ac-39b6-864c-49ed3bd2177a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "21cf3acc-2008-3d42-a9de-35ebed4594ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.12"}, {"id": "291c2f47-6cc4-3de1-8d22-1dc8c188ed23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d8be81735aa89413b333de488251f0e64e2be591 <28768bc7ea0b13f558a70f63cc3cfcd32d55d488"}, {"id": "2bcfcfc1-d1b9-3760-939a-ec49ebe8c4a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "647120c0-8ae7-3ef1-8847-76cb2cc27904", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "6d9ca9ff-dc0f-3b13-a674-95e14c5686ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d8be81735aa89413b333de488251f0e64e2be591 <2127e6b79d9d579ea538a350d1bbe859e39814d5"}, {"id": "6fcc28ec-0e62-325f-a212-0c98b44a127f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.14"}, {"id": "a0bead2b-b2ff-3364-8bda-6736e342c817", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d8be81735aa89413b333de488251f0e64e2be591 <bb37286db65368cb72ba8757ad86299c4e4a73fc"}, {"id": "ad274a96-8c86-30f6-a31d-59152f49afc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d8be81735aa89413b333de488251f0e64e2be591 <a6fc88b22bc8d12ad52e8412c667ec0f5bf055af"}, {"id": "bec7f21f-b371-3036-9e7a-4d3628c15bf2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "d4dcde35-23d3-3f91-89cc-677f4758e2c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "ff025008-23b7-3925-bc40-27db234a9010", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d8be81735aa89413b333de488251f0e64e2be591 <20b98d9ffb09763048a7c84b47403eb0f177272c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cbf72c05-09cf-3b71-a9a0-c60a85c1abf6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}